::PC_U03_L03_GP_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U03_L03_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.TR.7
Question:
In Trigonometric Equation Strategies, which response best shows mastery of MLA.PC.TR.7?
{
=A. Use equation solving, show the work, and explain the conclusion with evidence#Correct. This is the strongest response because it names the lesson concept, shows the reasoning, and connects the conclusion back to MLA.PC.TR.7.
~B. Start calculating before identifying the trigonometric equations or the required feature#Incorrect. This is a misconception because calculation alone can answer the wrong question. First identify the trigonometric equations and the feature being assessed. Review the lesson concept before trying a similar item.
~C. Use a related term from unit circle support without checking whether it answers the question#Incorrect. This confuses related vocabulary with the actual target of the question. Use the lesson definition and check that the conclusion matches MLA.PC.TR.7. Review the lesson concept before trying a similar item.
~D. Give only a final answer without connecting the result to the lesson standard#Incorrect. This skips the explanation requirement. A mastery response must include reasoning so the Teacher of Record can see how the answer was found. Review the lesson concept before trying a similar item.
}
